# What Prettier is allowed to own.
#
# Only the code that a formatter can usefully decide: `.ts`, `.astro`, `.mjs`,
# the JSON config files, and the two YAML-ish deployment files. Everything else
# in this repository is either generated, machine-local, or deliberately
# hand-set — see the reasons below each entry.

# Build output, dependencies, generated stylesheet.
dist/
node_modules/
.astro/
.npm-cache/
src/skins/.generated/

# Machine-local. Real conversation text and ~100MB of screenshots live here;
# nothing in it is published, so nothing in it needs a house style.
.local/

# Screenshot passes and reference captures — binary, ~62MB.
docs/shots*/
docs/ref/
public/plates/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Print sheets and probe pages: hand-set, and Prettier makes them worse.
#
# `skin.css` (up to 3000 lines across five skins) and `base.css` are typography
# and grid rules written one declaration per line by hand — `.cropmarks .tl {
# top: 14px; left: 14px; }` on one line because that is how you read a set of
# four corners. Prettier explodes each of those into four lines, and the diff is
# a few thousand lines that changes no rendered pixel. The files are instead
# governed by `npm run check` (tokens, colour containment) and by the probes,
# which is the only governance that matters for CSS here.
#
# The probe pages are the same argument with a shorter history: each is a
# throwaway harness written to answer one question, most are under 150 lines,
# and none of them ship (`scripts/*.html` is excluded from the Docker image).
# Formatting them would produce churn in files whose whole purpose is to be
# read once and then either kept as evidence or deleted.
*.css
scripts/*.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prose. Prettier reflows Markdown and aligns tables to the widest cell, which
# turns a one-line edit into a whole-table diff. The four root guides are read
# by humans on GitHub and are not code; the editor decides their shape.
*.md

# npm's own file. `npm install` rewrites it with its own formatting.
package-lock.json
